<!--
    kuna-elfgot-noreturn: a call to an import through its .got slot takes the
    import's no-return flag, and the slot's address stays an address.

    Issue: a `-fno-plt` build (or a linker-relaxed `call *slot(%rip)`) calls an
    import through its GLOB_DAT slot in `.got`; there is no PLT stub. The slot
    was named for the import but the no-return list was matched only against
    functions and PLT stubs, so a function ending in `abort()`/`exit()` ran on
    into the next function until funcboundflow truncated it, and the
    call-graph propagation never saw a wrapper ending in such a call.

    Stage / sub-stage: P1 external-refinement (`kuna-analysis`
    `loader/noreturn.rs` flags the slot, `analyzers/noreturn_propagate`
    reads calls through a flagged slot) and P9 (`coreaction_render.rs
    (is_pointer)` keeps a constant equal to an import slot a constant).
    Strict fixes, no option.

    Fixtures: `elf_got_noreturn_x86_64` (gcc -O2 -fPIC -pie -fno-plt; `check`
    ends in a GOT call to `abort`, `die` in a GOT call to `exit`, and `pick`
    reads a function pointer from a `.data.rel.ro` table filled by the same
    kind of relocation outside `.got`); `elf_got_slotaddr_x86_64` takes the
    ADDRESS of the `lgetxattr` and `getxattr` slots (`lea sym@GOTPCREL(%rip)`)
    and jumps through the one it selects; `elf_got_noreturn_aarch64`
    (clang -O2 -fPIC -fno-plt, lld) reaches `exit` through `adrp/ldr/blr`.
-->
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x100000" readonly="true">
c3
</bytechunk>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x100000" name="harness_stub"/>
</binaryimage>
